! Basin-hopping input taken from the Wales group LJ38 introduction.
! The driver appends one RANSEED line per run.
! GMIN's SW keyword selects the native Stillinger-Weber silicon in the
! reduced units sigma and epsilon, the units of examples/h2h_covalent.
! TEMPERATURE is the reduced 0.2 Yoo and Zeng used for basin hopping on
! these clusters, J. Chem. Phys. 119, 1442 (2003). The 1.0 of the
! Lennard-Jones file fragments them: the adaptive step grows past the
! 1.8 sigma cutoff and quenches end on separated atoms.
! MONITOR, DUMPINT and TRACKDATA are omitted. They schedule output.

SLOPPYCONV 5.0D-3
TIGHTCONV 1.0D-3
EDIFF 0.003
MAXIT 600 500
SAVE 2
CENTRE
SORT

TEMPERATURE 0.2
STEPS 90000000 1.0
STEP 0.40 0.51
NEWRESTART 40
AVOID 4.0 20 F
SW
